Fixed. The bug was in `advanceTurn` at src/sim.ts:43 — the growth check used `foodSurplus >= 0`, so a settlement where production exactly equals consumption (surplus of 0) still gained +1 population every turn, and settlements with a deficit that only reaches zero after carry-over never grow, but break-even ones did.

The fix changes it to `foodSurplus > 0`, so population grows only when there's an actual surplus this turn.

Verified: `npm run test` (4 tests pass) and `npm run typecheck` both succeed.


